  "title": "Bring the cluster-P Riemann-Roch substrate into AJC",
  "objective": "Give Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge the strongest honest Riemann-Roch and vanishing substrate available for the committed Picard representability route. Cluster P consists of the Euler-characteristic ledger, section-drop results, and uniform H1 vanishing needed downstream. AJC already contains a substantial sorry-free adelic lane, including RiemannRoch/Adelic/ChiLedger.lean, but the sibling Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild contains a broader sorry-free 17,792-line RiemannRoch development. In particular, AJCR RiemannRoch/UniformVanishing.lean proves a single-field bounded vanishing core; it does not by itself supply field-extension uniformity or global generation.\n\nThe owner of this task should decide, theorem by theorem, whether to reuse AJC code, port an AJCR result, adapt its argument, or rederive it in the AJC abstractions. Report that provenance honestly and do not promise a mechanical port. The one already identified open AJC leaf in this cone is principal-divisor degree zero in RiemannRoch/WeilDivisor.lean. Work may close it when it materially advances the shared substrate.\n\nThis task owns only AlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/** in AJC and may read AJCR without modifying it. It must not edit Picard/RigidPushforward files, Jacobian.lean, AbelJacobi.lean, the root import roll-up, or blueprint files. Notify ajc-gate when a vanishing or cohomology theorem becomes available so that gate hypotheses can be removed. Ask ajc-truth to add final root imports and to audit axioms of major landed results.\n\nDone means the strongest reachable cluster-P statements are present under AJC-compatible hypotheses, focused Lean checks and the appropriate project build pass, no new anonymous or misleading sorry boundaries are introduced, #print axioms results are reported, and every remaining gap distinguishes single-field vanishing, extension-uniformity, and global generation precisely.",
